But you have to wipe your shoes. Come on in. I was just not talking to my wife.

505
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:36,240
Can I get you something?

506
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:38,240
Please be careful. He'll shoot.

507
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:41,240
Well, he got some extra zagini here if that's what you're after.

508
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:45,240
Yeah, that's right. You do as you're told. Nobody's going to get hurt.

509
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:48,240
You cross us up.

510
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:52,240
The old lady's dead. Am I getting through to you?

511
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:55,240
I'm thinking it over.

512
00:24:55,240 --> 00:24:58,240
If you harm my wife, I'll kill you.

513
00:24:58,240 --> 00:25:00,240
This is like an elderly strada.

514
00:25:00,240 --> 00:25:02,240
Don't make me harm, Pa.

515
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:05,240
We'll do anything you say. Tell them we'll do anything they say, Tom.

516
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:07,240
All right, sir.

517
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,240
We'll do anything you say.

518
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:11,240
How many rooms you got in this place?

519
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:13,240
Just this here and two bedrooms.

520
00:25:13,240 --> 00:25:15,240
And, of course, the rumpus room.

521
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:17,240
Anybody else live here with you?

522
00:25:17,240 --> 00:25:19,240
No. Well, Franz leaves.

523
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:22,240
What about company? You expecting anybody to come here?

524
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:23,240
My son.

525
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:25,240
Mike Tyson.

526
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:27,240
That him?

527
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:29,240
No, he's actually more three-dimensional.

528
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,240
Where's he now?

529
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:33,240
He goes to an agricultural college upstate.

530
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:37,240
This is coming home tomorrow for the Thanksgiving holidays.

531
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:40,240
I hope he's got sense enough not to start any trouble.

532
00:25:40,240 --> 00:25:42,240
Well, let him.

533
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,240
That's one thing I can handle.

534
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:46,240
He won't cause any trouble.

535
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,240
How long are you planning to stay?

536
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:50,240
Until we get work.

537
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:52,240
It's not a problem. Are you getting tired of us already?

538
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:55,240
We'll let you know how long.

539
00:25:55,240 --> 00:25:57,240
Probably just through the high holidays.

540
00:25:57,240 --> 00:25:59,240
It depends.

541
00:25:59,240 --> 00:26:02,240
Well, if you're planning to spend the holiday, I'll need some help.

542
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:04,240
Mother, no.

543
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:05,240
Father and I always set a full table.

544
00:26:05,240 --> 00:26:07,240
Big deal, holiday.

545
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:10,240
Don't you believe in them, child?

546
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:12,240
Well, sure.

547
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:15,240
Every day is going to be Thanksgiving from now on.

548
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:18,240
Well, we'll need a lot of turkeys.

549
00:26:18,240 --> 00:26:20,240
I'll help if I may.

550
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:22,240
Thank you. What's your name?

551
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:24,240
Susie Sikophon.

552
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:24,240
Jane.

553
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:26,240
Hey, go on over there and sit down.

554
00:26:26,240 --> 00:26:28,240
Okay.

555
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:30,240
You keep them covered while we look around.

556
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:30,240
Right.

557
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:33,240
Sit down, doll.

558
00:26:33,240 --> 00:26:35,240
You're the one.

559
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:37,240
You might as well know we got a murder up against us,

560
00:26:37,240 --> 00:26:39,240
so we got nothing to lose.

561
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:42,240
Well, I just put up some peach preserve.

562
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:45,240
She's so crazy, she just might do it.

563
00:26:45,240 --> 00:26:48,240
You can use that phone to call the cops,

564
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:51,240
or you can tip them off to us when they come prowling around.

565
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:54,240
But Mike and I aren't going to be taken alive.

566
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:56,240
I'm stoic.

567
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:56,240
Believe me, that's level.

568
00:26:56,240 --> 00:26:59,240
That goes for you too, little flower.

569
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:01,240
You're in this just as deep as we are.

570
00:27:01,240 --> 00:27:03,240
I saw Mike kill a man.

571
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:05,240
I'll be a witness to it if I ever get the chance.

572
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:07,240
Remember that.

573
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:07,240
Oh, that's right. We should kill you then.

574
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:10,240
All of a sudden, you got things to say.

575
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:14,240
What makes you think you'll ever get a chance to be a witness?

576
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:17,240
Fascinating, Captain.

577
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:20,240
Anyone for gravy?

578
00:27:20,240 --> 00:27:22,240
Go ahead.

579
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,240
Make my-- oh, sorry.

580
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:26,240
You'd be doing me a favor.

581
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:26,240
Well, that's different.

582
00:27:26,240 --> 00:27:30,240
Try me again.

583
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:32,240
Later.

584
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:35,240
I gotta say, this isn't anything like the time we had

585
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:38,240
the Symbionnes Liberation Army over here.

586
00:27:40,240 --> 00:27:43,240
I hope he doesn't look at my fine washables.

587
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:45,240
There's a whole nother room in there.

588
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:47,240
There's a window in that bedroom where you can watch

589
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:49,240
every approach to the house for a mile.

590
00:27:49,240 --> 00:27:51,240
We picked the greatest baby.

591
00:27:51,240 --> 00:27:53,240
I'm on a total high about that window.

592
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:55,240
Hey.

593
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:57,240
You guys rotate crops?

594
00:27:57,240 --> 00:27:59,240
Hey, what's that down there?

595
00:27:59,240 --> 00:27:59,240
Storm cellar.

596
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:01,240
We use it for a storage room.

597
00:28:06,240 --> 00:28:08,240
There's an East Village coffee house down there.

598
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:10,240
Right down there?

599
00:28:10,240 --> 00:28:12,240
Yes. There's a switch on the wall there behind you.

600
00:28:12,240 --> 00:28:15,240
Really a mess down there. Sorry about that.

601
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:20,240
You really put up a lot of pickle tomatoes this year.

602
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:24,240
I've smelled enough.

603
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:27,240
Don't! Don't do that!

604
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:31,240
Well, we killed about five seconds.

605
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:33,240
The car pulls up. We have some company.

606
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:36,240
We all go right down there.

607
00:28:36,240 --> 00:28:38,240
Take little Grandma with us.

608
00:28:38,240 --> 00:28:40,240
She's my grandma?

609
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:42,240
And Pop?

610
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:44,240
You can either forget we're there.

611
00:28:44,240 --> 00:28:46,240
Or you can squeal on us.

612
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:48,240
Deal with her.

613
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:50,240
I can tell you right now, I wouldn't do anything

614
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:52,240
to put my wife in danger.

615
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:54,240
Not even to see that you get what's coming to you.

616
00:28:54,240 --> 00:28:58,240
Well, then, we're all going to get along just fine and dandy.

617
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:00,240
Oh, there might be some tension at first.

618
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:02,240
Well, I'm just a child. I'm hungry.

619
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:04,240
Come on, Grandma.

620
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:07,240
You want to help? Go ahead. You're the domestic type.

621
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:11,240
Better get a couple of those fryers out of the icebox, Tom.

622
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:13,240
And plenty of milk.

623
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:15,240
They're just downright impolite.

624
00:29:15,240 --> 00:29:17,240
It's not a farmer. It's the country ain't it?

625
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:19,240
I like milk.

626
00:29:19,240 --> 00:29:22,240
He's got a bum stomach, nerves.

627
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:24,240
And take it easy on the seasoning, too, Grandma.

628
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:27,240
I wouldn't waste seasonings on you thugs.

629
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:30,240
Huh? What's it doing?

630
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:36,240
That means something. I know it.

631
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:38,240
That's our ring.

632
00:29:38,240 --> 00:29:40,240
If we don't answer, it's going to make a lot of people

633
00:29:40,240 --> 00:29:42,240
might be suspicious.

634
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:44,240
That's a party like a dozen hicks listening in.

635
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:47,240
That means we can't take a chance on phoning out.

636
00:29:47,240 --> 00:29:49,240
We don't need to call us hicks, son.

637
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:52,240
We may live in the country, but...

638
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:55,240
What would you say?

639
00:29:55,240 --> 00:29:57,240
Oh.

640
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:59,240
Hello. Tom Grant speaking.

641
00:29:59,240 --> 00:30:03,240
Hello, Dad. This is Ben. How's everything?

642
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:05,240
Oh. Fine.

643
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:07,240
Good. I'm just clearing up here

644
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,240
so I can leave for the farm first thing in the morning.

645
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:11,240
Anything special you want me to bring home, Dad?

646
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:13,240
What? Can't think of a thing, son.

647
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:15,240
I just thought I'd check to see if you forgot anything.

648
00:30:15,240 --> 00:30:16,240
How's Mom?

649
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:18,240
I'm being held hostage. She's fine.

650
00:30:18,240 --> 00:30:20,240
Then we'll see you tomorrow.

651
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:24,240
Yeah, we'll expect your home about 11.30.

652
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:26,240
All right, son. Goodbye.

653
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:28,240
Help!

654
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:31,240
Ben says hi and don't have fun till he gets here.

655
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:33,240
Isn't that real cool, Dad?

656
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:37,240
You keep that up. The only one who's going to get it in the next, the turkey.

657
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:40,240
Don't mock turkeys.

658
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:42,240
Why a waggon?

659
00:30:42,240 --> 00:30:46,240
You got a real nice tablecloth here, Pop.

660
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:48,240
And I ought to get Al out here.

661
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:49,240
What'd you tell him?

662
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:51,240
They get a car and pick us up.

663
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,240
Here.

664
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:54,240
A couple of high crews.

665
00:30:54,240 --> 00:31:00,240
Want to play Scrabble or something after this?

666
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:02,240
Ow, ow, ow.

667
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:05,240
Richly satisfying.

668
00:31:05,240 --> 00:31:08,240
Pop, your chairs are too hard. You know that?

669
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:10,240
Don't mark my chairs too, son.

670
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,240
Too old-fashioned.

671
00:31:11,240 --> 00:31:14,240
I listened to Snoop Doggy Dog. Does that help?

672
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:17,240
You ain't hospitable, Pop.

673
00:31:17,240 --> 00:31:20,240
I'm a Midwesterner. What do you want from me?

674
00:31:20,240 --> 00:31:23,240
You're going to get a visit from a salesman, you know that?

675
00:31:23,240 --> 00:31:25,240
Not Herbalife again.

676
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:27,240
Only this guy, we don't hide from him.

677
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:29,240
He's invited.

678
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:31,240
I got a hand up to you, Mike, the way you use your head.

679
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:32,240
Here's your paycheck.

680
00:31:32,240 --> 00:31:34,240
Hey, little flower.

681
00:31:34,240 --> 00:31:36,240
Your boyfriend, Al.

682
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:39,240
If he stopped, he's a salesman. Call on a customer.

683
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:41,240
Yeah, how about that, Pop?

684
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:43,240
You would've said, "Buy a chicken feet.

685
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:45,240
First-class stuff for your charge."

686
00:31:45,240 --> 00:31:47,240
You want to unpack that one for me, son?

687
00:31:47,240 --> 00:31:49,240
I'm going to take this away. That's what you want, ain't it, Pop?

688
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:51,240
So, what do we mail this letter?

689
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:53,240
It's a box out on the road.

690
00:31:53,240 --> 00:31:55,240
What does that put in the city?

691
00:31:55,240 --> 00:31:57,240
Tomorrow, I suppose.

692
00:31:57,240 --> 00:31:59,240
All right, Pop.

693
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:01,240
Come on. Give me company.

694
00:32:01,240 --> 00:32:03,240
Well, I think we need some time apart.

695
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:06,240
I get a loan, so I need a lot of company.

696
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:08,240
After you, Pop.

697
00:32:08,240 --> 00:32:12,240
I'm not a violent man, but if you take my last stamp, I'll kill you.

698
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:15,240
So long, Sarah. I'll send help.

699
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:20,240
No much about farm cooking?

700
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:22,240
No, I don't.

701
00:32:22,240 --> 00:32:24,240
Well, it's bland, and there's lots of it.

702
00:32:24,240 --> 00:32:26,240
We can ourselves. Even churn our own butter.

703
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:27,240
In our pants.

704
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,240
We live simply.

705
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:31,240
I'll send you next to copy. The farm is almanac for that.

706
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:32,240
I get it, Bant.

707
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:35,240
It wouldn't hurt you. I need to learn something about a kitchen.

708
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:38,240
What makes you think I couldn't handle it if I wanted to?

709
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:41,240
There's a churn with a hand dasher over there.

710
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:43,240
Plenty of cream if you want to help.

711
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:46,240
Oh, no. You got it wrong. You're working for me.

712
00:32:46,240 --> 00:32:48,240
Can I have the day off?

713
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:57,240
Want to know something?

714
00:32:57,240 --> 00:32:59,240
I used to cook whole meals for families.

715
00:32:59,240 --> 00:33:00,240
Wow.

716
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:02,240
That's right. Me, little Terry.

717
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:03,240
No higher than that.

718
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:06,240
They had me washing and cooking and scrubbing all the time.

719
00:33:06,240 --> 00:33:10,240
There's a difference between working for strangers and working in your own home.

720
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:12,240
What do you mean, strangers? My sisters.

721
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,240
Four of them.

722
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:16,240
Each one taking me on for what they could squeeze out of me

723
00:33:16,240 --> 00:33:18,240
and passing me on to the next one.

724
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:19,240
Now, cry me a river, dear.

725
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:22,240
Check that fairy tale, Cinderella. No kidding.

726
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:25,240
Scullery maid. That's what I was.

727
00:33:25,240 --> 00:33:26,240
Where were your parents?

728
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:28,240
Six feet under.

729
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:29,240
Oh, they were miners.

730
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:30,240
Accident?

731
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,240
No, thanks.

732
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:33,240
Yeah, real accident.

733
00:33:33,240 --> 00:33:35,240
They were almost as old as you are when I was born.

734
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:36,240
How's that for breaks?

735
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:38,240
Oh, my God. That's old.

736
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:41,240
So don't give me any of this bunk about the home.

737
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:43,240
Also, you're my share of cheap.

738
00:33:43,240 --> 00:33:45,240
Born in the wagon of a traveling show.

739
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:48,240
That way I'm saving my nail polish for the ball.

740
00:33:48,240 --> 00:33:51,240
I change from scullery maid to Cinderella.

741
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:53,240
And midnight ain't never coming.

742
00:33:53,240 --> 00:33:56,240
I think you lost your allegory. It's off the track.

743
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:58,240
What are you doing to that chicken? Cream-aiding it? Hurry it up.

744
00:33:58,240 --> 00:34:01,240
Well, I'm extruding it if you don't mind.

745
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:05,240
Hey, Mike, you think they'll talk about us on television?

746
00:34:05,240 --> 00:34:07,240
Big shots now.

747
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:08,240
They don't get it.

748
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:10,240
Stick with us, little Eva.

749
00:34:10,240 --> 00:34:12,240
You'll be able to buy your own butter already made up.

750
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:13,240
No kidding.

751
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:15,240
We'll be rolling in loot.

752
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:20,240
What are you going to do with all the money you didn't get for killing that deputy?

753
00:34:20,240 --> 00:34:22,240
You talk too much.

754
00:34:22,240 --> 00:34:26,240
I've been wondering, Jane, you weren't really with him, were you?

755
00:34:26,240 --> 00:34:27,240
No.

756
00:34:27,240 --> 00:34:30,240
I just happened to be in the wrong place at the wrong time.

757
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:32,240
Why don't you close your yap?

758
00:34:32,240 --> 00:34:33,240
Shut your pie hole.

759
00:34:33,240 --> 00:34:35,240
Doesn't make any difference.

760
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:37,240
Nobody believes it anyway.

761
00:34:37,240 --> 00:34:38,240
I sure don't.

762
00:34:38,240 --> 00:34:40,240
I think I do, Jane.

763
00:34:40,240 --> 00:34:42,240
Okay, so you believe her.

764
00:34:42,240 --> 00:34:44,240
I can stop wondering so much.

765
00:34:44,240 --> 00:34:46,240
You wonder about us country folks.

766
00:34:46,240 --> 00:34:48,240
We wonder about your city folks.

767
00:34:48,240 --> 00:34:50,240
Could I have some pie?

