I want to make faces as she rises in pain.

2110
01:24:59,340 --> 01:25:01,340
So you made it after all.

2111
01:25:01,340 --> 01:25:03,340
Rot in hell, Tala.

2112
01:25:03,340 --> 01:25:07,340
Hey, cop, that'll even ever figure out any of this.

2113
01:25:07,340 --> 01:25:09,340
Hey, that's not fair. I helped a little.

2114
01:25:09,340 --> 01:25:12,340
We just took her along for the ride.

2115
01:25:12,340 --> 01:25:14,340
Oh, don't mean to rush her, ma'am.

2116
01:25:14,340 --> 01:25:17,340
This death can take long, thanksgiving and all.

2117
01:25:17,340 --> 01:25:19,340
[sobbing]

2118
01:25:19,340 --> 01:25:22,340
I'm dying in your son's pants.

2119
01:25:22,340 --> 01:25:24,340
Nobody ever cried for me before.

2120
01:25:24,340 --> 01:25:26,340
Argentina?

2121
01:25:26,340 --> 01:25:28,340
I think she's got more lines, ma'am.

2122
01:25:28,340 --> 01:25:30,340
Should I work the mouth?

2123
01:25:30,340 --> 01:25:43,340
Look to this day, graduate, as you plunder the world.

2124
01:25:43,340 --> 01:25:46,340
[sobbing]

2125
01:25:46,340 --> 01:25:48,340
Oh, go ahead. Let it out.

2126
01:25:48,340 --> 01:25:50,340
Have a teenage cry wave.

2127
01:25:52,340 --> 01:25:54,340
Wow. Now, there's an upbeat ending for you.

2128
01:25:54,340 --> 01:25:56,340
Yeah. Zingo.

2129
01:25:56,340 --> 01:25:58,340
[sobbing]

2130
01:25:58,340 --> 01:26:00,340
Does not justify the means.

2131
01:26:00,340 --> 01:26:16,340
Wow, Crow.

2132
01:26:16,340 --> 01:26:18,340
That movie posed so many difficult questions,

2133
01:26:18,340 --> 01:26:21,340
yet at the same time left so many things unanswered.

2134
01:26:21,340 --> 01:26:24,340
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

2135
01:26:24,340 --> 01:26:26,340
So, letters?

2136
01:26:26,340 --> 01:26:27,340
Yeah. Right.

2137
01:26:27,340 --> 01:26:29,340
Hey, isn't it Tom's turn to get them?

2138
01:26:29,340 --> 01:26:31,340
Mail call, mail call.

2139
01:26:31,340 --> 01:26:32,340
Oh, brother.

2140
01:26:32,340 --> 01:26:33,340
Robot, Crow thee.

2141
01:26:33,340 --> 01:26:34,340
Yeah.

2142
01:26:34,340 --> 01:26:35,340
They didn't get Squawk, Crow.

2143
01:26:35,340 --> 01:26:37,340
My guess is you skew lousy with women and young men.

2144
01:26:37,340 --> 01:26:39,340
But we'll put together some focus groups

2145
01:26:39,340 --> 01:26:40,340
and ferret that out for you.

2146
01:26:40,340 --> 01:26:42,340
Sirbo, can we just have the mail, please?

2147
01:26:42,340 --> 01:26:44,340
Keep your flight suit on, Nelson.

2148
01:26:44,340 --> 01:26:46,340
And just what kind of a name is Nelson anyway?

2149
01:26:46,340 --> 01:26:48,340
You're not russian by any chance, are you, comrade?

2150
01:26:48,340 --> 01:26:50,340
Keep those things.

2151
01:26:50,340 --> 01:26:52,340
All right. This first one is from,

2152
01:26:52,340 --> 01:26:54,340
oh, from Jim Pratt.

2153
01:26:54,340 --> 01:26:55,340
Could eat no food?

2154
01:26:55,340 --> 01:26:57,340
And why don't you put that up on Stillstore there?

2155
01:26:57,340 --> 01:26:59,340
They look the better clean.

2156
01:26:59,340 --> 01:27:00,340
Thank you. Jim Pratt.

2157
01:27:00,340 --> 01:27:02,340
Okay. Jim writes, "Dear Mike Crow,

2158
01:27:02,340 --> 01:27:04,340
Servo and the rest of the MST3K crew,

2159
01:27:04,340 --> 01:27:06,340
those of us who just finished watching

2160
01:27:06,340 --> 01:27:08,340
the Brain That Wouldn't Die experiment

2161
01:27:08,340 --> 01:27:10,340
here at the New Hampshire State Prison

2162
01:27:10,340 --> 01:27:13,340
all feel that Mike Nelson has potential."

2163
01:27:13,340 --> 01:27:14,340
Thank you. Thank you, Jim.

2164
01:27:14,340 --> 01:27:15,340
That's very nice.

2165
01:27:15,340 --> 01:27:17,340
Nelson, you got the prison vote.

2166
01:27:17,340 --> 01:27:19,340
Yeah. Well, it doesn't surprise me.

2167
01:27:19,340 --> 01:27:21,340
Your situations are similar.

2168
01:27:21,340 --> 01:27:24,340
Although, I imagine it's a little worse up here.

2169
01:27:24,340 --> 01:27:28,340
You know, no visitations, food's lousy.

2170
01:27:28,340 --> 01:27:32,340
Everything you know and love is thousands of miles away.

2171
01:27:32,340 --> 01:27:33,340
Yep.

2172
01:27:33,340 --> 01:27:35,340
But you got us.

2173
01:27:35,340 --> 01:27:37,340
That's right.

2174
01:27:37,340 --> 01:27:38,340
Isn't there another letter?

2175
01:27:38,340 --> 01:27:39,340
I hope so.

2176
01:27:39,340 --> 01:27:40,340
Yes, there is another letter.

2177
01:27:40,340 --> 01:27:43,340
This one is from Valerie Curiacopolis.

2178
01:27:43,340 --> 01:27:47,340
And I have an idea that maybe you could read this one, Tom.

2179
01:27:47,340 --> 01:27:49,340
I'll tell you that. I just will then.

2180
01:27:49,340 --> 01:27:51,340
Welcome, Mike. I'm glad you're on the S.O.L.

2181
01:27:51,340 --> 01:27:53,340
You'll definitely have your hands full up there.

2182
01:27:53,340 --> 01:27:55,340
But just remember, even though those bots

2183
01:27:55,340 --> 01:27:58,340
have been up there longer, you're bigger than them.

2184
01:27:58,340 --> 01:28:02,340
Just keep that in mind when...

2185
01:28:02,340 --> 01:28:04,340
You're bigger than some of us, Mike.

2186
01:28:04,340 --> 01:28:07,340
Yeah, just remember, Mike, if push came to shove,

2187
01:28:07,340 --> 01:28:08,340
I could take you.

2188
01:28:08,340 --> 01:28:09,340
Wow.

2189
01:28:09,340 --> 01:28:10,340
But I never would.

2190
01:28:10,340 --> 01:28:12,340
Oh, my scars!

2191
01:28:12,340 --> 01:28:16,340
Well, that's all from our round back down to you,

2192
01:28:16,340 --> 01:28:18,340
subterranean doey guys.

2193
01:28:18,340 --> 01:28:20,340
That's right. I'm doey man.

2194
01:28:20,340 --> 01:28:23,340
I control the world supply of dairy products.

2195
01:28:23,340 --> 01:28:25,340
Steak is my ally.

2196
01:28:25,340 --> 01:28:26,340
Butter does my bidding.

2197
01:28:26,340 --> 01:28:30,340
Sour cream bows down before me in total abject terror.

2198
01:28:30,340 --> 01:28:33,340
Onion rings quake at my very...

2199
01:28:33,340 --> 01:28:41,340
[screaming]

2200
01:28:41,340 --> 01:28:43,340
[growling]

2201
01:28:43,340 --> 01:28:55,340
[music playing]

2202
01:28:55,340 --> 01:29:01,340
[groaning]

2203
01:29:01,340 --> 01:29:05,340
[screaming]

2204
01:29:05,340 --> 01:29:17,340
[music playing]

2205
01:29:17,340 --> 01:29:22,340
[groaning]

2206
01:29:22,340 --> 01:29:23,340
Oh!

2207
01:29:23,340 --> 01:29:49,340
[music playing]

2208
01:29:49,340 --> 01:29:56,340
[groaning]

2209
01:29:56,340 --> 01:29:58,340
Oh, for fuck's sake!

2210
01:29:58,340 --> 01:30:02,340
[screaming]

2211
01:30:02,340 --> 01:30:16,340
[music playing]

2212
01:30:16,340 --> 01:30:19,340
Oh, no, you don't, not this time!

2213
01:30:19,340 --> 01:30:21,340
[laughing]

2214
01:30:21,340 --> 01:30:26,340
[screaming]

2215
01:30:26,340 --> 01:30:37,340
[music playing]

2216
01:30:37,340 --> 01:30:44,340
[groaning]

2217
01:30:44,340 --> 01:30:46,340
Oh, huh.

2218
01:30:46,340 --> 01:30:48,340
TV's Frank, see me.

2219
01:30:48,340 --> 01:30:49,340
Dr. Forester.

2220
01:30:49,340 --> 01:30:51,340
I wonder what's going on.

2221
01:30:51,340 --> 01:30:52,340
Where'd she go?

2222
01:30:52,340 --> 01:31:01,340
[screaming]

2223
01:31:01,340 --> 01:31:13,340
[music playing]

2224
01:31:13,340 --> 01:31:23,340
[music playing]

2225
01:31:23,340 --> 01:31:33,340
[music playing]

2226
01:31:33,340 --> 01:32:00,340
[music playing]

2227
01:32:00,340 --> 01:32:03,340
[screaming]

2228
01:32:03,340 --> 01:32:04,340
To be on the other side.

2229
01:32:04,340 --> 01:32:05,340
Taylor!

